WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.240 --> 00:00:03.932
- [Narrator] This is the
Black Beauty Stick insect.

00:00:03.932 --> 00:00:07.670
A rare bug found only
in a tiny 12 acre area,

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.366
high in the remote
mountains of Northern Peru.

00:00:10.366 --> 00:00:12.949
(upbeat music)

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:18.550
Discovered in 2005,

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:21.400
the Black Beauty Stick Insect
has a velvet black body

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.830
covered in small bristles.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:24.910
The only other colors

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.780
on its body are its
piercing golden yellow eyes

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:29.710
and it's bright red wings.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:32.000
Not much is known about this species,

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.570
but scientists have observed
it to be most active at night,

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.160
when its deep black coloration,

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.230
keeps it hidden from predators.

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.090
In addition to its powerful
nighttime camouflage,

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:44.090
the Black Beauty Stick Insect is armed

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:46.070
with a gland at the rear of its head,

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:47.100
and when threatened,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.840
can spray a coercive,
strong smelling substance

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:50.850
at its attacker.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.770
Because their natural habitat is so small,

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:58.450
the Black Beauty Stick Insect’s
survival is precarious.

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.410
And because of its striking features,

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:03.560
they have become a popular
insect in the pet trade.

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.590
Luckily, due to successful
captive breeding efforts,

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:09.130
this particular threat
may be on the decline.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.945
This is the Black Beauty Stick Insect.

00:01:12.945 --> 00:01:15.528
(upbeat music)

00:01:19.435 --> 00:01:22.018
(tinkly music)

